# Keep the build context small and reproducible. Migrations are NOT ignored — the backend
# embeds them at compile time (sqlx::migrate!).
**/target
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
.github
.claude
docs
*.md
# Local dev-speed toolchain config: rolling nightly + rustc parallel front-end (`-Zthreads`) + the
# mold linker. These are nightly-only and need clang/mold on PATH, which the runtime image doesn't
# have — and the cargo-chef `cook` stage runs before rust-toolchain.toml would be copied, so it would
# hit stable and reject `-Z`. The code uses no nightly-only features, so the image builds cleanly on
# the base image's stable toolchain. (The CI test/lint job reads these files directly, unaffected.)
.cargo
rust-toolchain.toml
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
